<pre class=metadata>
Group: test
Shortname: test
Level: 1
Status: LS
ED: http://example.com/foo
Editor: Example Editor
Date: 1970-01-01
Title: Syntax Highlighting Features and All Built-in Languages
Abstract: Verifying markup inside highlighted code, highlight attribute cleanup and precedence, legacy highlighting, and syntax highlighting for every built-in language.
Legacy Highlights: ada
</pre>

<h2 id="markup">Markup in Highlighted Code</h2>

<h3 id="inside">Markup Inside Highlight Tokens</h3>

<p>Markup elements (e.g. <code>&lt;span></code>, <code>&lt;mark></code>) nested inside single tokens like keywords, identifiers, and strings:</p>

<pre highlight=js>
func<span>ti</span>on my<span>Func</span>tion() {
    con<mark>st</mark> str = "hel<span>lo</span> world";
}
</pre>

<h3 id="coincident">Markup Coincident with Highlight Tokens</h3>

<p>Markup elements whose boundaries exactly match token boundaries:</p>

<pre highlight=js>
<a href="https://example.com/const">const</a> <dfn export id="myidentifier">myIdentifier</dfn> = <mark>true</mark>;
</pre>

<h3 id="crossing">Markup Crossing Highlight Boundaries</h3>

<p>Markup elements spanning across multiple tokens or starting/ending mid-token:</p>

<pre highlight=js>
<a href="https://example.com/test">let a =</a> 1;
foo<mark>bar + baz</mark>qux();
/* A comment with <em>markup crossing</em> the comment */
</pre>

<h2 id="attributes">Highlight Attribute Cleanup, Precedence, and Legacy Fallback</h2>

<div highlight=js>
    <pre>
    const x = 1;
    </pre>
    <pre nohighlight>
    const y = 2;
    </pre>
</div>

<pre class="lang-py">
def foo():
    pass
</pre>

<pre class="lang-py" highlight=rust>
fn main() {}
</pre>

<pre class="lang-py" nohighlight>
def bar():
    pass
</pre>

<pre highlight=js>
<code nohighlight>const z = 3;</code>
</pre>

<pre nohighlight>
plain text
</pre>

<pre highlight=ada>
X := 42;
</pre>

